<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad ibn Qasim</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad ibn Qasim was an Umayyad general who conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sind">Sind</a> in the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus">Indus</a> valley around 711 to 712. His campaign brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> and Umayyad rule to part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-subcontinent">Indian subcontinent</a>. It was one of the eastern limits of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a>'s expansion.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/muhammad-ibn-qasim.jpg" alt="Muhammad ibn Qasim" width="320" height="157" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Umayyad_Caliphate_coinage_temp_Suleiman_ibn_Abd_al-Malik_al-Hind_(possibly_Multan)_mint._Dated_AH_97_(AD_715-6).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
